:: R5-NPC-RandomDonor [release5]
<<set $princessMaker99Seen to true>>
<<scene "img/ui/princessmaker99-donation.png" "$100. No message.">>

I scroll through the donation log. Most of the eight forty seven came in small amounts. Five, ten, twenty. The long tail of internet generosity. But a few stand out.

A hundred dollars from good_girl_energy. Message, "I literally created this account to donate to you tonight. I don't usually watch game streams. Your clip came across my timeline and I couldn't look away. Please don't stop."

Fifty dollars from thighHighKingdom. Message, "I've been a femboy for three years and watching someone discover it for the first time on stream gave me actual chills. Your face when you looked at yourself in the mirror at the start? That's the face. I know that face. Welcome."

Twenty five dollars from GhostReaper42. My five dollar regular. The one who's been donating since the early days. His message, "I've been giving you $5 a week for six months and tonight I gave you $25 and it felt more right than any of the $5s. I don't know what that says about me or you but I'm here for it."

Then there's the hundred dollars from someone I've never seen before. Username, PrincessMaker99. No message attached to the donation. Just the amount. A hundred dollars, dropped without a word, like a calling card left on a doorstep. I look at the profile. No other activity. Brand new account. Created tonight.

I note it and move on. I won't understand the significance for weeks.

<hr class="pt-hr">

<div class="pt-choices">
<<link "Before I sleep" "R5-SideQuest-ClipReview">><</link>>
</div>
